Icon sets for the 'marker-symbol' and 'stroke-symbol' attributes of a feature.

A value without a slash is an emoji character, and it is rendered with the image of the same
name in noto/. A value with a slash is the path of an icon, for example
/icon-sets/pinhead/cup_and_saucer.png. See app/javascript/helpers/functions.js (symbolUrl).

Sets in the emoji picker
------------------------

pinhead     CC0, https://github.com/waysidemapping/pinhead , the icon set of the map and the
            first category of the picker. It redrew Maki, Temaki and eleven more sources to
            one style, so those sets are not included separately any more.
noto        Noto Color Emoji, https://fonts.google.com/noto/specimen/Noto+Color+Emoji
            The picker reads noto/emoji-mart-data.json for its emoji categories.
openmoji    CC BY-SA 4.0, https://openmoji.org/ , an alternative rendering of the emoji set.
fontawesome CC BY 4.0, https://fontawesome.com/ , the free "solid" style only. The free
            package also has a "regular" (thin) style of the same icons and a "brands" style
            of colored logos, neither is in the index.

Every set except noto has an index.json, which the picker reads as one more category. To add a
set, add it to SETS in build_icon_sets.rb and to iconSets and categories in
app/javascript/controllers/feature/edit_controller.js. The script needs npm, inkscape and
imagemagick.

pinhead and fontawesome are monochrome SVG sets. The script downloads the npm package of a set
and rasterizes its icons to 72px PNG. It then keeps only the alpha channel, so that the icon is
white: a marker draws it on a circle in the color of the feature. A white icon needs a
background of its own on the page, see whiteIconSets in edit_controller.js.

Pinhead renamed the icons that it took over: maki 'cafe' is pinhead 'cup_and_saucer'. Its
dist/changelog.json records the source name per icon, and the script turns those names into
search keywords, so a search for 'cafe' still finds the icon. The same file gave the pinhead
ids in app/javascript/maplibre/import/google_icons.js.

openmoji is an emoji set of PNG files. The script builds its index from the names and the
keywords of noto/emoji-mart-data.json, and it takes the png of the same emoji character.

Emoji sets
----------

The emoji sets are downloaded by hand. Noto releases are at
https://github.com/googlefonts/noto-emoji/releases (directory png/72). OpenMoji releases are at
https://github.com/hfg-gmuend/openmoji/releases (directory color/72x72). After a download, the
script convert_to_emoji_names.sh renames the files from their code points to the emoji
character itself. .gitignore drops the files that keep their original name.
